ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57, D-94): large blurs at a reduced resolution, as Skia blurs
Library: resvg 0.48.1
Fixes: none (speed: a blur's cost grows with its sigma in pixels, and so with the zoom)
Upstream: none yet: to be proposed to linebender/resvg (ours)
Remove when: a resvg release blurs large sigmas at a reduced resolution, or this patch no longer applies

A blur whose sigma passes 4 pixels is computed on a copy reduced about 2^n times on that axis (each
reduced pixel the mean of the area it covers, edges on the region's), with a sigma of at most 4 there,
and enlarged back with bilinear interpolation (filter::blur()); a lone such blur of the whole region, on
a group with no clip path or mask, draws the group itself on the reduced layer, enlarged within the
filter region at full resolution (filter::reduction(), render::render_reduced()). The owner's artwork:
1.84 levels from Chromium (1.75 exact); resvg's references with blurs: at most 19 levels on a few pixels,
1.5 on average. Requires imageviewer-filter-area.patch and imageviewer-turbulence-cache.patch (their
Context and reach).

